    <h1>Rethinking What &ldquo;Secure&rdquo; Means in AI Systems</h1>
    <p class="lede">For two decades, &ldquo;secure&rdquo; meant defended boundaries and controlled access. Box&rsquo;s CISO argues that AI which <em>acts</em> &mdash; not just answers &mdash; breaks that model, and needs a new, testable definition built around behavior, intent, and runtime control.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <div class="m"><span>Source</span><strong>Box</strong></div>
      <div class="m"><span>Author</span><strong>Heather Ceylan, CISO</strong></div>
      <div class="m"><span>Topic</span><strong>Securing AI &amp; agents</strong></div>
      <div class="m"><span>Reading time</span><strong>6 min</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

